samqeq: lr-solve shielding = PQEq Gaussian erf(a_ij r)/r (param 4th col = Rc (Gaussian radius)); routed through compute_H + add_fixed_charge_field + the legacy gas path (calc_Hval)
fix_modify      chg energy yes
fix_modify      chg gself on width 1.0 types 1
samqeq: gself RESTRICTED to type(s) 1 -- the self-energy is a lattice regulariser (metal sites, where eta is a bulk TF quantity with no width in it) and a DOUBLE COUNT on molecular sites, whose eta was fit to the IP/EA of a finite-width atom
samqeq: gself ON -- finite-width charge self-energy K_e*sqrt(2a/pi) ADDED to the on-site diagonal (width 1.000 A for the listed type(s) only); folded into eta from eta0 at init()
fix_modify      chg ridge eig 1000.0 200
samqeq: ridge mode = Lanczos lambda_min: ridge = max(lr_ridge, 1000 + 0 - lambda_min) eV (floor + delta), 200 Lanczos steps, recomputed every 1 step(s) (continuous in config; matrix kept PD). The Ritz estimate is an UPPER bound on lambda_min: an unconverged m can only MISS a negative mode, never invent one -- m >= 60 recommended for interface cells; delta is the estimate-error budget, so lambda_min(A+ridge) >= floor whenever the estimate is within delta of the true value
